    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463-a3">

                <pb facs="0634" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg538"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Michaels to Mr. Smith.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I herewith beg to reply to your note asking
                    me why my wife did not leave for Paris as soon as she received her passport.</p>
                <p>She could not go, as she caught a severe cold and could not travel and I could
                    not leave her alone. When neither of us could leave the news came that our dear
                    boy was out of danger.</p>
                <p>When she can travel she proposes to join the boy and take him to the seaside.
                    Herewith I beg to inclose the doctor’s certificate of her illness, and, if
                    necessary, I can get one from Paris concerning the boy.</p>
                <p>Yours, truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Michaels.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
